    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1093">

                <pb facs="0907" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Bacon, Leonard Lee: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-04">August 4,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received August 4—4:27 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1712. Re Deptel 479, July 23 [<hi rendition="#italic">22</hi>]<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d1093-f1"/>. Bacon’s application exit permit via Tientsin,
                    destination Dairen by way of Tokyo, filed August 3. Application received for
                    consideration only. Statement made that foreigners travel Nanking-Tientsin not
                    yet authorized. Similar statement made to AMilAt<anchor n="49" xml:id="d1093-f2"
                    /> Beebe August 1.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1712 repeated Peiping 317 Dairen 46.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
